-Before Play Mode, the Editor automatically repairs missing Timeline chrome/templates in **Edit Mode**. Runtime UI generation is still disabled. The repaired objects remain in the scene and are editable.
+Before Play Mode, the Editor automatically repairs missing Timeline/Preview chrome and templates in **Edit Mode**. The application shell remains scene-authored. In addition, `PreviewPanel` now has a narrow runtime self-repair fallback that creates only missing Preview children (content, toolbar controls, layers, or the light template) when a partially broken scene reaches Play Mode. The repaired Editor objects remain in the scene and are editable.
 
 Persistent Timeline / Preview / application UI references are serialized on their components. After the references have been captured, moving or renaming those referenced GameObjects does not break initialization. Scenes produced by the previous revision are migrated by recursive name lookup when the serialized references are initially empty.
 
